      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Major changes in our understanding of congestive heart failure have resulted from an etiologic shift, identification of neurohormonal effects, and a realization of the importance of diastolic dysfunction. Accordingly, management has changed. Digitalis should be avoided with diastolic dysfunction. When the dysfunction is systolic, a regimen of digitalis, diuretic and ACE inhibitor may be optimal."},
